              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কাঁকড়া (kā̃kṛā) (kāṁkṛā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from karkaṭa, \"crab\" (CDIAL 2816). CDIAL lists Bengali kāṁkṛā, \"crab\", and suspects that the Sanskrit word is itself of non-Aryan origin."
